{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/66881-crazy-or-onto-something-my-idea-for-a-mummy-story","id":66881,"title":"Crazy or onto something? My idea for a Mummy story","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-06T18:52:03-08:00","id":66881,"title":"Crazy or onto something? My idea for a Mummy story","content":"This occurred to me almost immediately after reading the opening quote in the first chapter of Guildhalls of the Deathless. It's the one about a Gestapo officer playing chess with Bruno Schulz's dad.<br /> <br /> My first thought was, &quot;Oh man, somebody mentioned having a game where their mummies were fighting some nazis who Did A Bad Thing and opened up the mummies' tombs. That'd be a sweet game.&quot;<br /> <br /> But my second thought was...more devious.<br /> <br /> Mummy(-ies) gets summoned to perform a task. But the summoner was not in fact one of their cultists....<br /> ...<br /> ...<br /> ...<br /> ...BUT A NAZI!<br /> <br /> That's actually a little bit of hyperbole, it doesn't have to be nazis, it can be any group that isn't the mummy's cult. Really my question is less, &quot;Lol nazi mummies&quot; and more:<br /> <br /> Can a Mummy be summoned by someone who is not one of their cultists to perform a task they find objectionable? Would this actually be an interesting setup? Is the mummy allowed to kill the one who summoned it without suffering the consequences, and is there a way for the summoner to keep itself safe?<br /> <br /> Then the story kept advancing in my head and the logical conclusion is that the mummy does the deed and starts losing Sekhem <i>like dang fast now y'all</i> but in the name of vengeance has to track down the summoner...though a mummy probably wouldn't care as much about revenge as it would starting a new cult so that it could be summoned again later after the offender was dead from old age anyway (of course, it could always be a Promethean or a Vampire, or even another Mummy?). So if you were using a mortal (though not necessarily non-supernatural) antagonist then you'd have to incense the players to hunt the antagonist down some other way. Stolen relic, maybe? In danger of being destroyed?<br /> <br /> I dunno, maybe I'm just up too late but my brain's abuzz trying to make this work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T06:09:20-08:00","id":67132,"title":"","content":"I think a mummy would have a pretty easy time spinning a &quot;summoning by a non-cultist&quot; into &quot;disturbing the tomb.&quot; But would they want to? Time awake is time awake, and a new summoner might be a road into a new cult (actually, for that very reason, even a newly-awakened Memory 0 mummy might instinctively know when this intruder is deliberately trying to make contact). And those Nazis who were into occult stuff were frequently into fringe archaeology as well, fertile ground for a mummy's influence. Whether or not the mummy would later decide that the Nazis are that appalling - or the Nazi decide that the mummy is insufficiently Aryan - is a matter for later on.<br /> <br /> Worth noting: some Nazi race theorists of the time believed that Germanic white people were <i>a</i> master race rather than <i>the</i> master race, and that there could be others - it's why Himmler was such a big fan of the Japanese (the Samurai were a big influence on how he conceived the SS) - and Nazis weren't immune to going ga-ga over Tibetans. It's not impossible that a Nazi fringe archaeologist might credit &quot;Iremite&quot; with being another master-race, and of which later Egyptians are a degradation.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T06:38:47-08:00","id":67159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/66881-crazy-or-onto-something-my-idea-for-a-mummy-story?p=67132#post67132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think a mummy would have a pretty easy time spinning a &quot;summoning by a non-cultist&quot; into &quot;disturbing the tomb.&quot; But would they want to? Time awake is time awake, and a new summoner might be a road into a new cult (actually, for that very reason, even a newly-awakened Memory 0 mummy might instinctively know when this intruder is deliberately trying to make contact). And those Nazis who were into occult stuff were frequently into fringe archaeology as well, fertile ground for a mummy's influence. Whether or not the mummy would later decide that the Nazis are that appalling - or the Nazi decide that the mummy is insufficiently Aryan - is a matter for later on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are good points, especially the &quot;time awake is time awake&quot; part. Depending on the Mummy I guess so long as the summoner doesn't act too arrogantly or entitled the mummy won't care. I'm just thinking about my usual players. Getting them to take Mummy seriously is already an uphill battle, and combine that with Nazis I think they'd assume it's time for a rip-roaring Nazi beat-'em-up from the start rather than waiting to see where it's going.<br /> <br /> Actually, one of my regulars already thinks Mummies fill the classical antagonist role too well to be appropriate PCs: they're powerful with wide-ranging influence and have a diverse array of servants of varying degrees of competence. To him that apparently screams &quot;Evil overlord&quot;.<br /> <br /> Going back, that could be an interesting game by itself: Mummies reject the summoner's requests and, uh, &quot;purge&quot; the area, then go about rebuilding or finding their cults.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Worth noting: some Nazi race theorists of the time believed that Germanic white people were <i>a</i> master race rather than <i>the</i> master race, and that there could be others - it's why Himmler was such a big fan of the Japanese (the Samurai were a big influence on how he conceived the SS) - and Nazis weren't immune to going ga-ga over Tibetans. It's not impossible that a Nazi fringe archaeologist might credit &quot;Iremite&quot; with being another master-race, and of which later Egyptians are a degradation. </div> </div> </div>Huh...that <i>is</i> worth noting. I also didn't know any of it. I like this idea of Nazi fringe archaeologists. Could you point me to more records about these guys, or is that as simple as a wikipedia check?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T01:03:24-08:00","id":67777,"title":"","content":"That's actually somewhat interesting...Compared to some of the shit the Iremites did to people in the past, forcing them into the Rite of Return, Slavery, all this other stuff...Would a Mummy REALLY find some of the stuff he's told to do in order to pursue a more stretched-out descent by an individual of the Third Reich all that heinous? They enslaved entire primitive cultures for an ideology, its not nearly such a far step for someone from that culture to go along with &quot;Killing these individuals is for the good of the Fatherland&quot;. Besides, how many people has the average Arisen killed in their assorted Descents already?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1645-autochthon","name":"Autochthon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T08:08:27-08:00","id":69084,"title":"","content":"Keeping some things in mind.. for one, its unlikely a given Mummy knows the context of world war 2 or nazis, and as the previous post said, Irem may have put the nazis to shame.. for two, as had been pointed out, the Nazis weren't against ANY pure race (such as Japan).. i'd say that could lead to the worlds sickest buddy movie. But unless my facts escape me, there is some ado in the book about the Maa'kep supporting Nazis and Illuminati and all that jazz. I run a cult summoning much the same as a disturbance of the tomb if the supplicant doesnt perform properly (and for every mummy, thats different based on their tastes).. so if the Nazi knows enough to be humble, cultist or not.. I'd allow it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T09:47:13-08:00","id":69151,"title":"","content":"Yeah, for the Nazi idea I've realized that it really doesn't work.<br /> <br /> That having been said, my original question of<br /> <br /> &quot;Can a mummy be summoned to perform a task that it finds objectionable, and what should a mummy do if it's put in such a situation? Go after the summoner first and take the Sekhem hit, then ignore the purpose while you try to (quickly) build a new, loyal cult with better security, or work towards the purpose in that irritatingly Unmotivated way while rebuilding a cult, then killing the summoner and taking whatever relic they used to summon you back?&quot;<br /> <br /> remains unanswered. I guess I'm asking how much can the Storyteller expect to get away with using summonings in a tricky/dickish way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T11:21:52-08:00","id":70730,"title":"","content":"I think it addresses that in the core book. Mummies still have to perform the duty (unless the Judges outright veto it, which is rare), but are then very likely to make their annoyance and displeasure known to the cultists. For example, the Mummy may have to fulfil the task, but if a summoner is not his cultist, the only thing stopping him from killing the fool for his audacity would be a Memory roll. In most cases, itd be like being haunted by a very powerful, and very material, ghost. Sure, the mummy will grant your wish for protection--but it will then sacrifice your family to his judge. sure, he will destroy your enemies, but once he is free he will destroy you, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}